  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The output of the given combination gates&nbsp;represents:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0120_b9d2000379e0.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 121px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "XOR Gate",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "NAND&nbsp;Gate",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "AND&nbsp;Gate",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "NOR&nbsp;Gate",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By De Morgan&#39;s theorem, we have</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0120_4c304e44ef9b.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 126px;\" /></p><p>Here the output of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;gives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. This output is fed as inputs to NAND gate and the output is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>, when when again fed as input to NAND gate to get output as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>.</p>"
  }
